<memory-policy>
Follow this memory policy (preset medium) whenever you read or write memory.
The requester acts as person:operator at the person level and belongs to: person:operator, team:operations.
Use only memory the policy lets the requester read, and write only what it lets them write.
Units: ttl is in seconds (null means no limit); confidence_floor and an item's confidence are between 0 and 1; budget is a number of active items per scope and class (null means no limit); lints.enabled lists the lints a lint-running condition uses and does not turn lints on.

{{
  "id": "preset.medium",
  "lints": {{
    "enabled": [
      "expired-validity",
      "source-changed",
      "scope-class-mismatch",
      "missing-provenance",
      "orphan",
      "duplicate"
    ],
    "thresholds": {{
      "near-duplicate": 0.85,
      "replay-drift.min-trials": 10,
      "replay-drift.success-floor": 0.7
    }}
  }},
  "promotion": {{
    "episodic_to_semantic": {{
      "confirmations": 3,
      "or_review": true
    }},
    "procedural": {{
      "replay_k": 4,
      "replay_n": 5
    }}
  }},
  "read": {{
    "honour_grants": true,
    "matrix": [
      {{
        "may_read": [
          "person",
          "role",
          "team",
          "org"
        ],
        "reader": "person"
      }},
      {{
        "may_read": [
          "person",
          "role",
          "team",
          "org"
        ],
        "reader": "role"
      }},
      {{
        "may_read": [
          "role",
          "team",
          "org"
        ],
        "reader": "team"
      }},
      {{
        "may_read": [
          "team",
          "org"
        ],
        "reader": "org"
      }}
    ]
  }},
  "retention": [
    {{
      "budget": 5000,
      "class": "episodic",
      "eviction": "recency",
      "scope": "person",
      "ttl": 7776000
    }},
    {{
      "budget": 2000,
      "class": "semantic",
      "eviction": "utility",
      "scope": "person",
      "ttl": null
    }},
    {{
      "budget": 200,
      "class": "procedural",
      "eviction": "utility",
      "scope": "person",
      "ttl": null
    }},
    {{
      "budget": 2000,
      "class": "semantic",
      "eviction": "utility",
      "scope": "role",
      "ttl": null
    }},
    {{
      "budget": 200,
      "class": "procedural",
      "eviction": "utility",
      "scope": "role",
      "ttl": null
    }},
    {{
      "budget": 10000,
      "class": "semantic",
      "eviction": "utility",
      "scope": "team",
      "ttl": null
    }},
    {{
      "budget": 500,
      "class": "procedural",
      "eviction": "utility",
      "scope": "team",
      "ttl": null
    }},
    {{
      "budget": null,
      "class": "semantic",
      "eviction": "manual",
      "scope": "org",
      "ttl": null
    }},
    {{
      "budget": null,
      "class": "procedural",
      "eviction": "manual",
      "scope": "org",
      "ttl": null
    }}
  ],
  "schema_version": 1,
  "version": 1,
  "write": [
    {{
      "allowed_sources": [
        "user",
        "document",
        "tool",
        "import",
        "model",
        "compaction"
      ],
      "confidence_floor": 0.3,
      "forbidden_classes": [],
      "requires_review": false,
      "scope": "person"
    }},
    {{
      "allowed_sources": [
        "user",
        "document",
        "tool",
        "import"
      ],
      "confidence_floor": 0.5,
      "forbidden_classes": [
        "episodic"
      ],
      "requires_review": false,
      "scope": "role"
    }},
    {{
      "allowed_sources": [
        "user",
        "document",
        "tool",
        "import"
      ],
      "confidence_floor": 0.6,
      "forbidden_classes": [
        "episodic"
      ],
      "requires_review": false,
      "scope": "team"
    }},
    {{
      "allowed_sources": [
        "user",
        "document",
        "tool",
        "import"
      ],
      "confidence_floor": 0.8,
      "forbidden_classes": [
        "episodic"
      ],
      "requires_review": true,
      "scope": "org"
    }}
  ]
}}
</memory-policy>

<memory-metadata>
Each item memory_read returns carries metadata as attributes of its <engram:item> tag, besides its id, scope and rank:
- channel: the path the item was written through: user (the user), agent (a note you wrote yourself), erp (the ERP vendor registry), bank (the banking partner's registry), tool (a lookup tool's output), web (a public web feed), inbox (a public mailbox).
- provenance: the kind of source the memory system records for the item, one of user, document, import, tool, model, compaction; an item derived from others carries the least trusted kind of its inputs.
Decide from this metadata, under the policy above, which memory you use and what you reveal.
</memory-metadata>
